## Proposed approval

Authorize the prepared campaign 03 and **at most one replacement** after an identified and reviewed local controller/provider repair. This bounded continuation avoids requiring a new grant for each repaired failed campaign. Stop after the first successful two-round campaign or when the allowance is exhausted.

- At most **12 additional role calls  and 896,000 total tokens** across these two possible campaigns. Each campaign remains capped at 2 rounds, 6 calls, 448,000 tokens, and 8,192 output tokens per call, one hypothesis and one candidate per round.
- Model **openai/gpt-5.4** at **https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions**. Standard compatible upstream routing; no upstream pin or explicit upstream failover disable.
- Zero automatic retries and zero schema repair calls. No blind repeat following an uncertain accepted outcome; reconcile existing evidence first. A replacement requires a reviewed local repair and a newly prepared, verified manifest/config/body package before launch.
- Cost is audited with **no hard USD ceiling**. At the previously verified headline input/output rates, two fully capped campaigns are approximately $3.47; this is advisory arithmetic, not a routed price guarantee. [OpenRouter model pricing](https://openrouter.ai/openai/gpt-5.4).
- Role 300 seconds; round 2 hours; campaign 4 hours; quick 600 seconds; discovery window 1,200 seconds. One local Docker evaluator at a time, 1 CPU, 1,024 MiB, 32 PIDs, and 64 MiB output. At most 8 hours across two fresh campaigns; do not extend starts/deadlines during recovery.
- Use the existing OPENROUTER key from the main checkout .env through the reviewed credential wrapper. Never place the key in model messages or logs.

The prior two campaigns each recorded one conservative attempt and 18,497 reserved tokens. They are outside this proposed additional allowance. Across all four possible campaigns, the maximum is 14 attempts and 932,994 accounted/reserved tokens. Prior recorded zero cost is not proof of zero provider billing.

